ScopeSeam shows where a package fits and where it does not as a band split navy and limestone: the ambient loop the package serves drawn whole in the navy half, a loop it cannot serve dashed in the limestone half, two tie-in nodes on the seam between them, the limit row on the seam itself and each half's rows numbered under its drawing.

- On the site: a `spec` block with `"look": "scope-seam"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-scope-seam.js`), on ind-personal-care "Where the package fits, and where it does not". Concept: pass 12 image 203, `design-system/inspiration/gemini/203-p12-ind-personal-care-fit.png`; its invented node tags and list words are not used: each loop is named by its half's first row.
- Markup: `section.aq-scope-seam-sec` (limestone, navy left half `::before`, `flow` seam rule `::after`) → `div.aq-scope-seam` (two columns) → `div.__in` (`__head`, `p.__side.is-in`, `figure.__fig.is-in` with `svg.__svg` and `figcaption.__lab`, `ol.__list.is-in`) and `div.__out` (`div.__seam` with `__nodes` and `p.__seamt`, `div.__limit`, `p.__side.is-out`, `figure.__fig.is-out`, `ol.__list.is-out`). Lists of `li.__item` (`__no`, `h3.__p`, `p.__v`, `p.__m`, `a.__link`).
- Fields: `h`, `intro`, `rows [{p, v, m, side, link, link_label}]` (side `package` | `site` | `limit`; default site), `sides [package label, site label]`, `seam`. The same fields as BatteryLimit, so the two swap freely; `cols`, `fold` and `fold_noun` are not read (every row shows).
- Tokens: `navy` / `limestone` grounds, `on-navy` and `on-limestone` text, `flow` seam, nodes and limit card edge, arrows `limestone` on navy. Titles 20/28, values 15/22, notes 14/20.
- **Phones** (≤ 860 px): the navy block (head, side label, package rows, then the ambient loop right on the seam) over the limestone block. The loop's two branches turn down (phone-only paths `.is-p`; desktop ones `.is-d`) and cross the seam's `flow` rule through its two nodes (90 % and 95 % of the drawing's width, `--fw`) into the dashed loop, whose tie-ins come down from above its top edge (the overrun is clipped at the seam); then the seam's name, the site label, the dashed loop, the limit card and the site rows. Limestone runs full bleed by a `border-image` outset (nothing above the seam). Tablets (600–860 px): drawings capped at 420 px. Every row shows (no fold). About 1,490 px at 375 and 1,330 at 768 with six rows.
- Dark: the site numerals 04–05 use `--on-limestone` (limestone stays light in dark; `--flow` would flip to 1.6:1).
- Use it for a scope boundary with conditions on each side. For site requirements against a battery limit, BatteryLimit.

## Motion

On scroll-in the ambient loop draws (DrawSVG 1.1 s), the tie-in nodes press onto the seam, the dashed loop fades in and its dashes creep once, the rows rise in. Once, under 3 s; nothing under reduced motion.
